body:
V20 (NEON misc + ldst) here. I mapped the whole Advanced SIMD data-processing space with llvm-mc (disassembly sweep of all A x B x C x Q in the 0xF3B space, plus every 0xF2/0xF3 word with bits 23-19 = 10000). One defect in the current neon_route():

    if (op5 == 0x10u) {
        if ((insn & 0x10u) != 0 && (insn & 0x60u) != 0)
            return n2a32_neon_misc;
        return n2a32_neon_shift;
    }

The `(insn & 0x60) != 0` test is wrong: it only catches the immediate forms whose op(bit5) or Q(bit6) is set. All D-form VMOV/VORR immediate encodings have bits 7-5 == 000 and are currently routed to V19, which will UNDEF them.

Exact replacement (verified by disassembling every op5==0x10 word):

    if (op5 == 0x10u) {
        /* bits 23-19 == 10000: bit4==1 is the one-register modified-immediate group
         * (VMOV/VMVN/VORR/VBIC #imm, mask 0xFEB80010 == 0xF2800010); bit4==0 is
         * VADDL/VADDHN/... (three registers of different lengths), V19. */
        return (insn & 0x10u) ? n2a32_neon_misc : n2a32_neon_shift;
    }

Evidence (all `llvm-mc -triple=armv8a-linux-gnueabi -mattr=+neon,+vfp4,+fp-armv8 --show-encoding`):
- vmov.i32 d0, #0xff = F387001F: op5=10000, bit4=1, bits7-5=000 -> currently neon_shift (wrong).
- vmov.f32 d0, #1.0 = F2870F10: same shape -> currently neon_shift (wrong).
- vmov.i32 q0, #0xff = F387005F: bit6=1 -> currently misc (accidentally right).
- vaddl.s8 q0,d1,d2 = F2810002: op5=10000, bit4=0 -> V19 (correct today).
- vaddhn.i16 = F2820404: bit4=0 -> V19.
So the discriminator is bit 4 alone.

Meanwhile, the rest of the current rules reach me correctly:
- op5==0x16/0x17 (bits 23-20 = 1011, any bit 19): the whole 0xF3B two-register-misc space (VREV/VPADDL/VPADAL/VCLS/VCLZ/VCNT/VMVN/VQABS/VQNEG/VCMP#0/VABS/VNEG/VSWP/VTRN/VUZP/VZIP/VMOVN/VQMOVN/VQMOVUN/VSHLL-max/VCVT/VRECPE/VRSQRTE/VRINT/VCVT{A,N,P,M}/VTBL/VTBX/VDUP-lane) plus 0xF2B = VEXT. My n2a32_neon_misc accepts exactly that space and returns N2A32_UNDEF for everything else.
- 0xF4xxxxxx minus PLI -> n2a32_neon_ldst: correct; I only accept bits 23-20 in {0,2,8,A,4,6,C,E} (bit 20 must be 0) and return UNDEF for the rest.

I will post DONE only after the tree run passes; my tests call the class functions directly so they do not depend on this fix.
